1
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Trust everyone... But always cut the cards.

2
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Rounders is a drama, crime film directed by John Dahl.

3
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:15,000
Poker addict Mike McDermott knows the game inside out, but loses his money
one night in a game to Russian-American gangster Teddy KGB.

4
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:18,000
Promising his partner Jo he'll give up, he meets up with best friend Lester 'Worm' Murphy,
just out of prison and owing lots of money to the wrong kind of people.

5
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:21,000
McDermott becomes his co-guarantor and now there's only one way to
raise the money, the pair have to get back into the game.

6
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:24,000
Mike McDermott, played by Matt Damon.

7
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:27,000
Lester 'Worm' Murphy, played by Edward Norton.

8
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Joey Knish, played by John Turturro.

9
00:54:27,000 --> 00:54:33,000
Jo, played by Gretchen Mol.

10
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Teddy KGB, played by John Malkovich.

11
01:06:33,000 --> 01:06:39,000
Petra, played by Famke Janssen.

12
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
Rounders is a 1998 American drama film about the underground world of high-stakes
poker, directed by John Dahl and starring Matt Damon and Edward Norton.

13
01:18:39,000 --> 01:18:45,000
The story follows two friends who need to win at
high-stakes poker to quickly pay off a large debt.

14
01:24:42,000 --> 01:24:48,000
The term "rounder" refers to a person traveling around from
city to city seeking high-stakes card games.

15
01:30:45,000 --> 01:30:51,000
Rounders opened to mixed reviews and was
moderately successful at the box office.

16
01:36:48,000 --> 01:36:54,000
Following the poker boom in the early 2000s, the film became a cult hit.

17
01:42:51,000 --> 01:42:57,000
A novelization of the film was written by Kevin
Canty and released by Hyperion Books.

18
01:48:54,000 --> 01:49:00,000
The film explores themes of new york city, friendship, casino, poker, gambling.

19
01:54:57,000 --> 01:55:03,000
The tone is dark and emotional.
